  "narrative": "**Where We Stand**\nWe opened tournament play with a strong 3-1 victory over the Nepean Wildcats, putting us tied at the top of Pool B with two points and advancing in 65 of the 81 remaining scenarios.\n\n**Our Next Game**\nWe are back on the ice tonight, Friday, October 16 at 9:15 PM, when we face off against the Belmont Blazers.\n\n**Around the Pool**\nBelmont also claimed two points today by edging out the Wilmot Wolverine 2-1, setting up a battle for first place in our matchup tonight while Wilmot and Nepean clash later at 9:45 PM.",
  "coaches_corner": {
    "don_cherry": "I tell ya right now, I told those Kanata Rangers girls to work their socks off, and DID THEY EVER\u2014knocking off Nepean 3 to 1! Shot blocking, backchecking, protecting their tender\u2014THAT is how you play real Canadian hockey, absolute BEAUTIES! Now bring on the Belmont Blazers and keep rolling, double thumbs up!",
    "for_game": "Belmont Blazers",
    "talking_points": "**Mindset**  \nThat big 3-1 victory over Nepean proved what happens when we play our game, so let's carry that momentum straight onto the ice. We set a high standard in our opener\u2014now it\u2019s about keeping our foot on the gas and staying relentless from the opening draw.\n\n**The Opponent**  \nBelmont is coming off a disciplined 2-1 win against Wilmot, proving they can protect a tight lead and play solid defense. They won't give us much room to breathe, so we need to fight for inner-slot ice and crash"
  },
  "tiebreaker_health": "In the 15 score-dependent scenarios, we hold a key tiebreaker advantage with our pool-leading +2 goal differential (GD) and 1 goal against (GA). Belmont is our primary rival at +1 GD and 1 GA, giving us a narrow +1 GD cushion. To guarantee advancement when tied on points, we must protect this margin by minimizing goals allowed and maximizing our scoring differential in our final game.",
